int bc_debug_finish(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Continues execution until the current function, subshell, or compound
command block returns, then stops.
The function sends a \f[CR]finish\f[R] command on \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R]
(channel 4).
.PP
The debugger records the current nesting depth and resumes execution.
When the depth decreases below the recorded level (i.e., the enclosing
block returns), a break\-hit event is generated for the next command at
the caller\(cqs level.
.PP
This is useful when you have stepped into a function and want to run the
rest of it without stopping, returning control to the caller.
.PP
The debugger mode changes to \f[CR]\(dqfinish\(dq\f[R] after this call.
.PP
