.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Breakpoints inside the finishing block still fire.
Finish is not a \(lqrun ignoring breakpoints\(rq command; it only sets
the depth threshold for the next automatic stop.
.IP \(bu 2
At top level (depth 0), there is no enclosing block to return from, so
\f[CR]finish\f[R] behaves like \f[CR]continue\f[R] and runs until the
next breakpoint or command completion.
.IP \(bu 2
The break\-hit event generated after finish fires at the first command
\f[B]after\f[R] the block returns, not at the return itself.
.IP \(bu 2
If the block calls \f[CR]exit\f[R], no break\-hit event is generated
(the session ends).
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
